IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gva-dates`
IMPORT `gva-core`

-- Graffiti Vandalism Act 2016 (WA) -- cases for the seat-neutral core (gva-core.l4).
--
-- Every expected value is worked by hand from the deposited text (registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_29645.txt), never
-- copied from the encoding's output. Days are counted under the Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(b): "within 28
-- days after" 1 March leaves 1 March out, so the 28th day is 29 March. Under s 61(1)(e) a last day on a Saturday,
-- Sunday or public holiday (Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 Second Schedule) moves to the next day that is not one:
-- 29 March 2027 is Easter Monday, so that last day is Tuesday 30 March. Weekdays are worked from 1 January 2027, a
-- Friday; Easter Sunday 2027 is 28 March.
--
-- A breached or still-pending DEONTIC cannot be asserted on the stable l4 (EVALTRACE ... EQUALS on a breached trace
-- fails both ways), so a regulative rule is asserted where its trace ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:"
-- line where it does not. Clock: days from the start of the rule (0), except the entry rule (minutes from the notice).
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the core`

`1 March 2027`  MEANS YearMonthDay 2027 3 1
`10 March 2027` MEANS YearMonthDay 2027 3 10
